From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 15:34:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 214/221] feat(area): align terrain to road editor action

"Align Terrain To Road" is a button on the Road component, declared through
IEditorActionComponent and run by CRoadAlignTerrainTool - the component form of
CRoadObject::AlignHeightMap (RoadObject.cpp:473-667).

Per heightmap cell inside the road's footprint: find the nearest place on the
road's centre line, take the road's own height inside width/2 + half a cell, blend
back to the terrain over Border Width with the raised-cosine falloff legacy uses
(:631-636), and leave everything beyond alone. Where legacy searches for the
nearest curve parameter with 24 rounds of a golden-section walk (:583-600), this
walks the component's own sample polyline - the same polyline the render nodes
were built from, so the answer needs no search and no second interpolation of a
curve the visible road does not follow either. One CHeightmap::RecordUndo over the
whole rectangle, so one Ctrl+Z puts the terrain back.

The road itself needs no rebuild afterwards: CTerrain::SetTerrainElevation
collects every eERType_Road node inside the changed rectangle and calls
OnTerrainChanged on it (terran_edit.cpp:407-421), and the component's nodes are
ordinary octree-registered road nodes.

THE PLUGIN NOW LINKS Sandbox, the CryDesigner way. CHeightmap is the editor's own
copy of the terrain - the one the level saves and the one the terrain undo stack
records - it is declared in EditorQt and exported with SANDBOX_API, and
EditorCommon has no terrain-writing interface at all (Cry3DEngine's
IEditorHeightmap is read-only). A component that changed only the engine's terrain
would lose the change on the next save. The price is that this DLL now has to be
rebuilt and deployed together with Sandbox.exe rather than on its own.

